WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
[suspenseful music fades in]

2
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
[suspenseful music intensifies]

3
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
[waves crashing]

4
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.000
[sinister beat]

5
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.000
[suspenseful music continues]

6
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.000
[wind blowing]

7
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.000
[waves crashing]

8
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Papa: Okay. Mind your fingers.

9
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.000
[clinking]

10
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Just like before, now.

11
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
[waves crashing]

12
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.000
[seagulls crying]

13
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.000
[glass clinks]

14
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.000
[higher tempo music fades in]

15
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.000
[suspenseful music]

16
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.000
[wind whistling]

17
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.000
- [sighs]
- [waves lapping]

18
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.000
[sinister music]

19
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.000
[waves crashing]

20
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.000
[dog panting]

21
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.000
[wave crashes]

22
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.000
[glass clinks]

23
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.000
[cork pops]

24
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.000
[liquid pouring]

25
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.000
[bottle clinks]

26
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.000
[sighs]

27
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
[dog whines]

28
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.000
What you looking at?

29
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.000
[clattering]

30
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.000
What are we gonna do today?

31
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Make yourself useful,
and give it some thought.

32
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.000
[clank]

33
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
[radio playing weather forecast]

34
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.000
[spoon clinks]

35
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.000
[suspenseful music]

36
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.000
Checkmate.

37
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.000
[sea roaring]

38
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.000
[creaking]

39
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.000
[sighs]

40
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.000
[snores lightly]

41
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.000
[coughs]

42
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Okay.

43
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.000
[sinister music resumes]

44
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.000
[exhales]

45
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.000
[groans]

46
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.000
[sea roaring]

47
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.000
Leave the crate
and come straight back.

48
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.000
The weather looks like
it's picking up.

49
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:57.000
- [boat crunching on sand]
- [wind whooshing]

50
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.000
[knocking on door]

51
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
[dog whines]

52
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.000
[knocking on door]

53
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.000
[sighs]

54
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.000
[wind howling]

55
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.000
[waves crashing]

56
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
[bottles clinking]

57
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Don't come up here again.

58
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.000
[slam]

59
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
[waves crashing]

60
00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Most people just say thank you.

61
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.000
[waves crashing]

62
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.000
[inhales] It's very important
that you listen.

63
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Don't ever
come up here again.

64
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.000
You know,
me and my uncle come up here

65
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.000
week after week,
bringing you supplies,

66
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.000
and yet you never even come down
to greet us.

67
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.000
Why is that?

68
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.000
[wind picking up]

69
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
[bottles clinking, box thumps]

70
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.000
[door slams]

71
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.000
[latch clanks]

72
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.000
[scoffs]

73
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.000
[shouts] I'm not afraid of you!

74
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.000
[suspenseful music]

75
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.000
[waves crashing]

76
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.000
[boat horn blows]

77
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.000
[wind howling]

78
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.000
[bottles clinking]

79
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.000
[waves churning, crashing]

80
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Man On Radio:
Message to all vessels.

81
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.000
Gale force winds are in
serious effect across the coast.

82
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.000
[breathing hard]

83
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Jessie, come on!

84
00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:20.000
- [waves crashing]
- [boat horn blares]

85
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:24.000
New storm formed now heading
towards the Hebrides.

86
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.000
[muffled radio message
continues]

87
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.000
[gasps]

88
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.000
[suspenseful music]

89
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.000
Don't give me that look.

90
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.000
[waves crashing]

91
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.000
[shouts] Jessie!

92
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.000
[groaning with effort]

93
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.000
[shouts] Come on!

94
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.000
[suspenseful music continues]

95
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.000
- [waves crashing]
- Papa!

96
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.000
[strains]

97
00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.000
[shouts] Come on!

98
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.000
[man talking on radio]

99
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.000
[sea raging, crashing]

100
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.000
Urgh!

101
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.000
[screams]

102
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.000
[gurgling]

103
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.000
[shouts] Jessie!

104
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.000
Uh... argh!

105
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.000
[wind whistling]

106
00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.000
[kettle whistling]

107
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.000
[dog whining]

108
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.000
[suspenseful music intensifies]

109
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.000
[kettle whistles louder]

110
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.000
- [high-tempo music]
- [grunts]

111
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
[waves crashing]

112
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.000
[straining]

113
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.000
[boat rumbling]

114
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.000
[boat motor starts, roars]

115
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.000
[gasps]

116
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.000
- [gurgling]
- [dramatic music]

117
00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.000
[splashing]

118
00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
[waves crashing]

119
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.000
[high-tempo music continues]

120
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.000
[gurgling]

121
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.000
[distorted gurgling]

122
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.000
[eerie music]

123
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.000
[high-tempo music resumes]

124
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.000
[distorted gurgling]

125
00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.000
[eerie music]

126
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.000
- [splashing]
- [gasping]

127
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.000
[suspenseful music]

128
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.000
[thunder cracks]

129
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.000
[groaning with effort]

130
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.000
[grunting]

131
00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.000
[dramatic music crescendo]

132
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.000
[dramatic music fades out]

133
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.000
[bed creaking]

134
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:28.000
Where's my uncle?

135
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.000
Where's my uncle?!

136
00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.000
[wind rattling windows]

137
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
He's dead.

138
00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.000
[gasps]

139
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.000
The trawler went down.

140
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.000
He was trapped.

141
00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.000
[sniffs]

142
00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.000
[melancholic music]

143
00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.000
[sobbing]

144
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.000
[waves crashing]

145
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:49.000
[dog panting]

146
00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Jessie: Agh!

147
00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:05.000
[inhales, grunts]

148
00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Agh!

149
00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:16.000
We need to get
the swelling down.

150
00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.000
[water dripping]

151
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.000
[gasps]

152
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.000
Why haven't you called anyone
about what happened?

153
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.000
Not even the police?

154
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:53.000
Who else knows we're here?

155
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:57.000
No one?

156
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.000
Just rest.

157
00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.000
Mason: [sighs]

158
00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
[sinister music]

159
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:23.000
- [cork pops]
- [drink pours]

160
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.000
[scoffs]

161
00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.000
You have to take me back.
You can't just keep me here.

162
00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:38.000
I... I mean, I... I don't even
understand why you're here.

163
00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.000
My uncle told me
that this lighthouse

164
00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.000
hasn't been working in years.

165
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.000
Yet you never leave here. Why?

166
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.000
My family will be
looking for me.

167
00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.000
You don't have a family.

168
00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:02.000
Your mother died
a few years back.

169
00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.000
Never knew your father.

170
00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.000
Your uncle's taken care of you
ever since.

171
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:12.000
Because there was no one else.

172
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.000
How do you know that?

173
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.000
Well, someone
will come looking.

174
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.000
[sighs]

175
00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.000
Will they?

176
00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.000
There's nothing here for anyone.

177
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.000
[sinister music continues]

178
00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.000
[door closes]

179
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.000
[winces]

180
00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.000
[drawer opens]

181
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:24.000
[music tempo increases]

182
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.000
[dog barking]

183
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.000
[door closes]

184
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.000
[sinister music]

185
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.000
[sniffs]

186
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:27.000
[dark music]

187
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.000
[whimpering]

188
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.000
[dog panting]

189
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.000
[whimpering continues]

190
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.000
[gasps]

191
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.000
[quietly] It's just a dream.

192
00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:17.000
[quietly] It's just a dream.

193
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:21.000
[exhales]

194
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.000
I know you're scared.

195
00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:28.000
And in a lot of pain.

196
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.000
When you use a weapon,

197
00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.000
you never operate from fear.

198
00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:45.000
Always balance your emotions.

199
00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.000
Keep your wits.

200
00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.000
Hold it like this.

201
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.000
Your thumb up against the hilt.

202
00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Tight in the palm.

203
00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.000
Hold it up.

204
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.000
Good.

205
00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.000
That's a strong grip.

206
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Good.

207
00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.000
I'm gonna look at your ankle.

208
00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.000
[dramatic music]

209
00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.000
[waves lapping]

210
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:03.000
[snaps] Come on.

211
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.000
- [sobs]
- [clattering]

212
00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:12.000
[high-tempo music fades in]

213
00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.000
[bowls, cutlery clatter]

214
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.000
[Jessie chattering]

215
00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:29.000
[radio chatter in background]

216
00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:37.000
How did you know my uncle?

217
00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.000
We served together.

218
00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.000
In the Royal Marines.

219
00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:46.000
He never told me your name.

220
00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:49.000
What is it?

221
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:52.000
Would it make a difference
if you knew it?

222
00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:56.000
Well, I'd at least know
what to call you.

223
00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:01.000
We're doing okay so far.

224
00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:07.000
Well, at least tell me
your dog's name, then.

225
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.000
He doesn't have one.

226
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:12.000
What?

227
00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:14.000
That's crazy.

228
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:17.000
Your dog doesn't even
have a name?

229
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:20.000
Well...

230
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:23.000
I'm going to call him...

231
00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:26.000
Jack.

232
00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:29.000
Right, Jack? Come. Hey.
[chuckles]

233
00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:31.000
[Jack panting]

234
00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:32.000
Jack.

235
00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:35.000
He likes the name Jack.

236
00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:37.000
Jack.

237
00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:49.000
Black Queen... to F2.

238
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.000
Check.

239
00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:53.000
[chuckles]

240
00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:57.000
You didn't tell me you could
play chess.

241
00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
You never asked.

242
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.000
Looks like I've got myself
a worthy opponent.

243
00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:05.000
Jessie: [chuckles]

244
00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:13.000
[radio continues in background]

245
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:18.000
[dramatic music]

246
00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.000
It's infected.

247
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:24.000
- Can't we just go to a hospital?
- No.

248
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:28.000
No.

249
00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:34.000
I'll get what's needed.

250
00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:41.000
[sea gushing]

251
00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:49.000
[suspenseful music fades in]

252
00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:44.000
[dramatic music fades in]

253
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:10.000
[dramatic music intensifies]

254
00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:25.000
[boat rumbling]

255
00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:26.000
[suspenseful music fades in]

256
00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:29.000
[traffic humming]

257
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:33.000
[tense music]

258
00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:37.000
[woman speaking indistinctly]

259
00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:40.000
[indistinct chatter]

260
00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.000
Woman: Ten years ago,
the Prime Minister

261
00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:59.000
assured this committee
and the nation

262
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:01.000
that her government, I quote...

263
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:04.000
"Was not and would not ever
collect data

264
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:06.000
on British citizens."

265
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:09.000
And yet, thanks to the recent
hack into MI6's servers,

266
00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:12.000
we have now learned that not
only has MI6

267
00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:15.000
been systematically harvesting
the personal information,

268
00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:18.000
calls, emails,
and voting patterns

269
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.000
of the British population,

270
00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:24.000
but has been doing so in order
to create an intelligence...

271
00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:26.000
super-system.

272
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.000
An advanced surveillance network

273
00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:32.000
called Total Human
Engagement Analytics,

274
00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:35.000
or more affectionately, THEA.

275
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Some of the details are,
of course, classified.

276
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:40.000
The essence of THEA is to make
better-informed decisions,

277
00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:44.000
to anticipate threats
more effectively.

278
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:47.000
Woman: What you've been doing
is unlawfully invading the life

279
00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:49.000
of every person
in this country.

280
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:52.000
Manafort: If they're innocent,
they have nothing to hide.

281
00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:54.000
Since THEA went online,

282
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:59.000
MI6 have intercepted threats
at a rate never before imagined.

283
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:02.000
Perhaps you could simply say
thank you.

284
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Let me be clear
on how this ends.

285
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:09.000
With you and Prime Minister
Fordham under investigation,

286
00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:12.000
and THEA dismantled.

287
00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:16.000
Haneron was grandstanding,
Prime Minister.

288
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:18.000
We both know the whole
thing's a circus,

289
00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:21.000
just without
the entertainment value.

290
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.000
Haneron is gaining traction
in this election.

291
00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:26.000
And this leak...

292
00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:29.000
it's a national embarrassment.

293
00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:32.000
We're gonna have to steady
the ship.

294
00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:33.000
[sighs]

295
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:36.000
You need a sacrificial lamb.

296
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:37.000
Let's face it, Stephen.

297
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:39.000
You're probably
the best spymaster

298
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.000
this country has ever produced.

299
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:45.000
But you are
a hopeless bureaucrat.

300
00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:48.000
We all have our shortcomings,
Prime Minister.

301
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:56.000
- [button clicks]
- PM: The tape's stopped.

302
00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:58.000
It's just the two of us now.

303
00:30:58.000 --> 00:30:59.000
[dramatic music]

304
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.000
I think this could be
a blessing.

305
00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.000
Really?

306
00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:07.000
To get you back into the shadows
where you belong.

307
00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:11.000
Could be our little secret.

308
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.000
Indeed, ma'am.

309
00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:16.000
Roberta Frost, your number two,

310
00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:18.000
she'll take over as head of MI6

311
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:20.000
as an interim appointment,

312
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:21.000
and then after the election,

313
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:24.000
I'll appoint somebody
more appropriate.

314
00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:26.000
Roberta's a good choice.

315
00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:30.000
She's a good team player.
And we don't want any outsiders.

316
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.000
Exactly.

317
00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:35.000
Enjoy your retirement.

318
00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:37.000
Thank you, Prime Minister.

319
00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:40.000
[suspenseful music]

320
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.000
How old is she?

321
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:52.000
About there.

322
00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:57.000
...like I said we were supposed
to go in the first place,

323
00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:59.000
but I thought we were gonna
go bowling instead.

324
00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:00.000
That's a bit more fun, no?

325
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.000
We always go...

326
00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:03.000
[suspenseful music continues]

327
00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:12.000
...like I said we were supposed
to go in the first place,

328
00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:13.000
but I thought we were gonna
go bowling instead.

329
00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:15.000
That's a bit more fun, no?

330
00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:17.000
[dark music]

331
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:22.000
[keyboard clacking]

332
00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:27.000
[beeping]

333
00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:30.000
Woman: High priority THEA alert.

334
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.000
We have a retinal match.

335
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:34.000
Timur Tchermoev.

336
00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.000
He's a high-value target,
wanted for the bombing

337
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:40.000
of our embassy in Algeria.

338
00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:43.000
His file is filled
with similar atrocities.

339
00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:44.000
Location?

340
00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:46.000
Stornoway. Outer Hebrides,
Scotland.

341
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:49.000
Repositioning satellites now.

342
00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:52.000
Who's our nearest assault team?

343
00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:54.000
Alpha.

344
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Send them.

345
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Mason: Okay.

346
00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.000
Let the medicine do its work.

347
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:07.000
That should be as good as new.

348
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:12.000
Thank you for the sweets,
by the way.

349
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.000
I got these.

350
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:24.000
I hope they're okay.
It's the best I could do.

351
00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.000
[poignant music]

352
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:44.000
I like them.

353
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:47.000
Thank you.

354
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:50.000
You're welcome.

355
00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:55.000
[sea churning softly]

356
00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:59.000
[music playing faintly
in background]

357
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.000
Mason: Mm.

358
00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:11.000
Smells good.

359
00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:22.000
So much better than porridge.

360
00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:26.000
That, young lady,
is a matter of opinion.

361
00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:30.000
[Jack panting, whimpering]

362
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:36.000
[waves crashing distantly]

363
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:40.000
What?

364
00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:44.000
- [cutlery clanking]
- [chair clatters]

365
00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:55.000
[sinister music]

366
00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:02.000
[chair scrapes]

367
00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:11.000
[boat engine roaring]

368
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:22.000
What's happening?

369
00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:24.000
Get in the bathroom.

370
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:25.000
Lock the door.

371
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.000
Don't make a sound.

372
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:30.000
Don't come out until
I come for you.

373
00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.000
Do it, Jessie.

374
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:36.000
[Jack whimpering]

375
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:41.000
Stay.

376
00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:45.000
[door closes, locks]

377
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:49.000
[clattering]

378
00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:58.000
[high-tempo music]

379
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:07.000
[metal clatters]

380
00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:16.000
Commando 1: Weapons free.
Kill target on sight.

381
00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:19.000
[panting over radio]

382
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:29.000
[whipping, rumbling]

383
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
[steel ropes whipping, crashing]

384
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:36.000
- Agh...
- [ropes whipping]

385
00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:40.000
- Argh...
- [splashing]

386
00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:43.000
Find this fucker.

387
00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:45.000
[high-tempo music intensifies]

388
00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:50.000
[switch, lights clanking]

389
00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:08.000
- [high-tempo music continues]
- [gunfire erupts]

390
00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:11.000
[whimpers]

391
00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:14.000
Spread out. Box him in.

392
00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:36.000
[high-tempo music continues]

393
00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:46.000
- [glass shattering]
- [grunting]

394
00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:50.000
- [flare gun fires]
- [screaming]

395
00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:01.000
[clattering]

396
00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:05.000
[grunting]

397
00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:08.000
[thumping]

398
00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:10.000
[body thuds]

399
00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:13.000
[high-tempo music intensifies]

400
00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:19.000
[Jack growls]

401
00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:22.000
[panting]

402
00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:24.000
[barking]

403
00:38:24.000 --> 00:38:28.000
- [Jack snarling]
- [man groaning]

404
00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:31.000
- [Jack snarling]
- [Jessie sniffling]

405
00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:33.000
[gunfire]

406
00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:36.000
[breathing heavily]

407
00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:39.000
[banging]

408
00:38:39.000 --> 00:38:41.000
[door smashes]

409
00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.000
Drop it! Jesus Christ!

410
00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:44.000
[struggling]

411
00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:49.000
I've found the girl.
Extracting her now.

412
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:52.000
Jack!

413
00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:57.000
[music intensity fades]

414
00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:03.000
- [smashing]
- Argh!

415
00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:06.000
[grunting]

416
00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:09.000
[sinister music]

417
00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:26.000
- [struggling]
- [blows landing]

418
00:39:26.000 --> 00:39:29.000
Aaargh! Argh!

419
00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:33.000
[knife blade swishes]

420
00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:36.000
- [gunshot]
- [thump, crash]

421
00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:40.000
[smash, wood splintering]

422
00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:41.000
[Jessie struggling]

423
00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:42.000
[sinister music]

424
00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:45.000
Let me go!

425
00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:51.000
- [gunshot]
- Argh!

426
00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:55.000
[gunshot]

427
00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:59.000
[coughing, gasping]

428
00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:06.000
[gasping]

429
00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:13.000
Jessie: Who is that? Who?

430
00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:19.000
Who... who are these guys?

431
00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:21.000
[gasps]

432
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:23.000
[suspenseful music]

433
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.000
Who... yeah, who are...?

434
00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:32.000
I need you to wait here.

435
00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:34.000
Nothing's gonna happen.

436
00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:36.000
I'm coming right back.

437
00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:40.000
But... but where are you going?

438
00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:45.000
[gasping, crying]

439
00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:47.000
[small waves breaking]

440
00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:54.000
[melancholic music]

441
00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:57.000
[gun clanks on floor]

442
00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:01.000
[sighs]

443
00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:17.000
Sorry, old boy.

444
00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:22.000
[sighs]

445
00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:28.000
[drawer opens]

446
00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:41.000
I'm off the reservation.
With baggage.

447
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:44.000
Okay, I'll be there.

448
00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:50.000
- [suspenseful music]
- [waves lapping]

449
00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:53.000
- [gasps]
- It's time to leave.

450
00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:55.000
[coughs] But w-what about Jack?

451
00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:57.000
Mason: Come on.

452
00:41:57.000 --> 00:42:00.000
Wha... what? What?

453
00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.000
Jack? No, no!

454
00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:04.000
Jack?

455
00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:07.000
[high-tempo music]

456
00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:10.000
Come on, we need to leave.

457
00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:12.000
[boat motor revving]

458
00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:25.000
[suspenseful music]

459
00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.000
Aziz: Alpha team, come in.

460
00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:32.000
They're all gone.

461
00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:34.000
Deakins: Who the hell
is this guy?

462
00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:36.000
Whoever he is,
he's not Tchermoev.

463
00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:40.000
Who's our nearest
tier-one asset?

464
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:42.000
[keyboard clacking]

465
00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:44.000
Workman.

466
00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:48.000
[exhales] Activate him.

467
00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:52.000
And notify all QRF teams
in the region to be on standby.

468
00:42:52.000 --> 00:42:55.000
Find out who that girl is.

469
00:42:56.000 --> 00:42:58.000
[dark music]

470
00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:05.000
[phone beeps]

471
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:07.000
[Velcro rips]

472
00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:10.000
[breathing heavily]

473
00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:13.000
[tense music]

474
00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:18.000
[high-tempo music]

475
00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:21.000
[wake splashing]

476
00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.000
Come on!

477
00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:40.000
- You're hurt!
- I'll be fine.

478
00:43:40.000 --> 00:43:42.000
But... but you're bleeding.

479
00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:44.000
Come on.

480
00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:57.000
[breathing heavily]

481
00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:02.000
- [dogs barking distantly]
- Stay behind me.

482
00:44:09.000 --> 00:44:12.000
I need to check something.
Wait here.

483
00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:16.000
[sheep bleating]

484
00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:26.000
I need to go inside.

485
00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:28.000
Get the keys.

486
00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:30.000
You mean steal them?

487
00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.000
Hey, I need you to wait here.

488
00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:37.000
Ever use a gun?

489
00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:39.000
I shot squirrels
with my uncle's air rifle.

490
00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:41.000
Good enough. Hold this.

491
00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:44.000
One hand there, and one there.

492
00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:45.000
Hold it tight against your body.

493
00:44:45.000 --> 00:44:47.000
Keep the barrel pointed
to the dirt.

494
00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:49.000
Keep your finger
off the trigger.

495
00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:51.000
It's sensitive.

496
00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:54.000
Get your back against the fence.

497
00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:17.000
[Velcro rips]

498
00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:19.000
[sniffs]

499
00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:35.000
[keys jangling]

500
00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:39.000
[sheep bleating]

501
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:02.000
- [door opens]
- [suspenseful music]

502
00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:04.000
[whispers] Hey, hey.

503
00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:06.000
That's as far as you go.

504
00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:10.000
[sinister music]

505
00:46:10.000 --> 00:46:12.000
Put it down.

506
00:46:15.000 --> 00:46:17.000
Please.

507
00:46:18.000 --> 00:46:20.000
[whispers] Whoa!

508
00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:24.000
Let's... let's go slow, hey?

509
00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:29.000
He's hurt. Can you help him?

510
00:46:29.000 --> 00:46:32.000
[sinister music intensifies]

511
00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:36.000
[door beeps, opens]

512
00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:37.000
What am I looking at?

513
00:46:37.000 --> 00:46:40.000
Timur Tchermoev.
His profile's been altered.

514
00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:42.000
See here?

515
00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:45.000
The code's been manipulated
to hide someone else.

516
00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:48.000
So, when a camera captures
the real person...

517
00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:49.000
Mm-hmm.

518
00:46:49.000 --> 00:46:51.000
...it misidentifies him
as Tchermoev.

519
00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:53.000
It's very sophisticated stuff.

520
00:46:53.000 --> 00:46:56.000
Whoever did this
used self-deleting code.

521
00:46:56.000 --> 00:46:58.000
[keyboard tapping]

522
00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:03.000
That's our guy.

523
00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:05.000
Roberta: Michael Mason.

524
00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:06.000
He's one of ours?

525
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:08.000
Yeah.

526
00:47:08.000 --> 00:47:10.000
But there aren't many details.

527
00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:12.000
He... he was orphaned.

528
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:14.000
Former SBS operator.

529
00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:16.000
K.I.A. ten years ago.

530
00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:18.000
Apparently not.

531
00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:22.000
Why would someone want to frame
one of our own to be targeted?

532
00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:24.000
- I don't know.
- [keyboard clacking]

533
00:47:24.000 --> 00:47:26.000
Whoa.

534
00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:29.000
I... I just tried to access
his mission logs from Poole,

535
00:47:29.000 --> 00:47:31.000
- and I got this.
- [dark music]

536
00:47:31.000 --> 00:47:34.000
[beep]

537
00:47:36.000 --> 00:47:38.000
Roberta: [sighs]
Okay, keep digging.

538
00:47:38.000 --> 00:47:40.000
Boy: There's a man
and a girl in our house.

539
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:42.000
Oh, the ops room just
intercepted a 999 call

540
00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:45.000
from a farm in Scotland,
matching Mason and our girl.

541
00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:49.000
Call the ops room.
Let them know I'm on my way.

542
00:47:49.000 --> 00:47:51.000
- We're all good, sir.
- Thank you, Ross.

543
00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:53.000
[sinister music]

544
00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:06.000
[keyboard clacking]

545
00:48:13.000 --> 00:48:15.000
Shit.

546
00:48:17.000 --> 00:48:20.000
[sinister music]

547
00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:22.000
Boy: They have guns.
Please help.

548
00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:24.000
They're holding my father.

549
00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:25.000
Our target is not
who we thought.

550
00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:27.000
His name is Michael Mason.

551
00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:28.000
I want him caught
and brought in for questioning.

552
00:48:28.000 --> 00:48:30.000
- Where's my asset?
- Workman's en route.

553
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.000
Boy: Please, please help.

554
00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:35.000
Workman.

555
00:48:35.000 --> 00:48:36.000
Good.

556
00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:38.000
[keyboard clacking]

557
00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:40.000
[exhales]

558
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:45.000
[phone beeps]

559
00:48:53.000 --> 00:48:56.000
[keyboard clacking]

560
00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:58.000
[high-tempo music intensifies]

561
00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:01.000
[beeps]

562
00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:06.000
[keyboard clacking]

563
00:49:15.000 --> 00:49:18.000
Fuck you, Mason.

564
00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:25.000
I'm... I'm not sure how good
this will hold.

565
00:49:25.000 --> 00:49:27.000
I've only stitched goats
and sheep.

566
00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:29.000
I'm sure it's good.

567
00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:30.000
- [chair scrapes]
- Thanks.

568
00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:33.000
- We'll get out of your hair.
- Man: Okay.

569
00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:42.000
I'm gonna need your truck.

570
00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:44.000
Man: Keys are by the front door.

571
00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:46.000
Go grab them, start it up.

572
00:49:46.000 --> 00:49:49.000
[quietly] I don't want you
to hurt them.

573
00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:53.000
I'm not gonna hurt them. Okay?

574
00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:57.000
Where's your son?

575
00:49:57.000 --> 00:49:59.000
Callum!

576
00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.000
Callum!

577
00:50:09.000 --> 00:50:12.000
Did you just go do something?

578
00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:14.000
[sheep bleats distantly]

579
00:50:14.000 --> 00:50:17.000
Callum?

580
00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:18.000
I called the police.

581
00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:21.000
[suspenseful music]

582
00:50:23.000 --> 00:50:25.000
- [dogs barking]
- [police siren wailing]

583
00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:27.000
Let's move.

584
00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:29.000
Come.

585
00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:30.000
Sit there. Don't move.

586
00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:34.000
[police sirens wailing]

587
00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:39.000
Deakins:
Local authorities are responding

588
00:50:39.000 --> 00:50:41.000
to a home invasion at the farm.

589
00:50:41.000 --> 00:50:43.000
Well, tell them not to engage.

590
00:50:43.000 --> 00:50:45.000
Deakins: Hold a perimeter.

591
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:48.000
Do not engage.
I repeat do not engage!

592
00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:50.000
We have personnel en route.

593
00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:52.000
[shouting]

594
00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:54.000
- Police!
- Are they going to arrest you?

595
00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:57.000
It's not the police
I'm worried about.

596
00:50:57.000 --> 00:50:59.000
[quietly] This way. Go, go, go.

597
00:50:59.000 --> 00:51:02.000
Hey, hey, wait.
Don't open the door!

598
00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:04.000
- I live here...
- [gunshot]

599
00:51:04.000 --> 00:51:07.000
[gunfire]

600
00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:09.000
[high-tempo music]

601
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:13.000
- [gun firing]
- [glass shatters]

602
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:15.000
Roberta: Find out
where those shots came from!

603
00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:17.000
I'm sorry.

604
00:51:17.000 --> 00:51:20.000
You need to stay here.

605
00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:22.000
Come on.

606
00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:23.000
[sinister music]

607
00:51:23.000 --> 00:51:24.000
Man: He's inside!

608
00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:26.000
Police!

609
00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:30.000
Put the weapon down!

610
00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:31.000
[grunting]

611
00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:34.000
- Drop the weapon!
- [grunting]

612
00:51:34.000 --> 00:51:35.000
[gasps]

613
00:51:35.000 --> 00:51:38.000
- Agh! Argh!
- Ugh! Urgh...

614
00:51:41.000 --> 00:51:43.000
Come on.

615
00:51:43.000 --> 00:51:45.000
Officer: Huh, uh!

616
00:51:47.000 --> 00:51:50.000
[police shouting]

617
00:51:55.000 --> 00:51:57.000
- Hey, police. Stop!
- [spraying]

618
00:51:57.000 --> 00:51:59.000
- Aargh!
- Drop the weapon!

619
00:51:59.000 --> 00:52:00.000
[taser fires]

620
00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.000
One to echo.
We have multiple men down.

621
00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:05.000
[car revving]

622
00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:06.000
[keys jangle]

623
00:52:06.000 --> 00:52:07.000
Woman On Radio:
They're rolling out.

624
00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:09.000
Hold your ground...

625
00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:10.000
Get in the back.
Keep your head down.

626
00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:12.000
Policeman: Get on Mason!

627
00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:13.000
Patch me through to Workman!

628
00:52:13.000 --> 00:52:15.000
[high-tempo music]

629
00:52:15.000 --> 00:52:17.000
Deakins:
He's turned off his comms.

630
00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:19.000
What the fuck is going on?

631
00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:21.000
Stay down and hold on.

632
00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:25.000
- [engine starts]
- [officers shouting]

633
00:52:25.000 --> 00:52:27.000
[cars smash]

634
00:52:27.000 --> 00:52:28.000
[gasping]

635
00:52:28.000 --> 00:52:29.000
[shouting in background]

636
00:52:29.000 --> 00:52:31.000
[engine revving loudly]

637
00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:33.000
[glass shattering]

638
00:52:33.000 --> 00:52:36.000
Officer On Radio: Bravo
two-one, we need backup immediately!

639
00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:41.000
[whimpers]

640
00:52:41.000 --> 00:52:44.000
[car revving]

641
00:52:56.000 --> 00:52:58.000
- [cars smash]
- [Jessie screams]

642
00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:00.000
[gasps]

643
00:53:05.000 --> 00:53:08.000
[cars revving full speed]

644
00:53:10.000 --> 00:53:12.000
- [gun fires]
- [Jessie screaming]

645
00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:18.000
- [cars collide]
- [grunts]

646
00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:23.000
[whimpers]

647
00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:41.000
[yelps]

648
00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:43.000
[tires squealing]

649
00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:06.000
Ah! Uh...

650
00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:14.000
[gasps, whimpering]

651
00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.000
[screams] Agh!

652
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:26.000
[cars crashing]

653
00:54:27.000 --> 00:54:30.000
[Workman grunts]

654
00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:37.000
- [gunfire]
- [Jessie screaming]

655
00:54:39.000 --> 00:54:41.000
[window shatters]

656
00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:46.000
Ugh!

657
00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:51.000
[smashing, crashing]

658
00:54:51.000 --> 00:54:54.000
[police car engine revs]

659
00:54:58.000 --> 00:55:01.000
- [dramatic music]
- [both groaning]

660
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:05.000
[tires spinning]

661
00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:06.000
[engine revving]

662
00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:09.000
[breathing heavily]

663
00:55:11.000 --> 00:55:13.000
[engine revving]

664
00:55:15.000 --> 00:55:17.000
[fence smashing]

665
00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:19.000
[suspenseful music]

666
00:55:29.000 --> 00:55:32.000
[clattering, banging]

667
00:55:36.000 --> 00:55:39.000
[brakes squeal]

668
00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:44.000
We're switching cars.

669
00:55:44.000 --> 00:55:46.000
Let's go.

670
00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:51.000
[hissing]

671
00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:54.000
[breathing heavily]

672
00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:02.000
[dramatic crescendo]

673
00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:06.000
- [birds twittering]
- [music fades]

674
00:56:17.000 --> 00:56:19.000
- Woman In Car: Excuse me.
- [police siren wailing]

675
00:56:19.000 --> 00:56:21.000
Are you okay?

676
00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:27.000
[suspenseful music]

677
00:56:27.000 --> 00:56:29.000
- Sir, stand still...
- [gunfire]

678
00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:31.000
[woman gasps in panic]

679
00:56:31.000 --> 00:56:33.000
[cries out]

680
00:56:39.000 --> 00:56:42.000
- [sighs]
- [sinister music]

681
00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:49.000
[tapping buttons]

682
00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:51.000
[line ringing]

683
00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:55.000
Manafort: Hello, Roberta.

684
00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:58.000
You calling to rub salt
in the wound?

685
00:56:58.000 --> 00:56:59.000
Roberta: Hardly, sir.

686
00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:01.000
For what it's worth,
I think the Prime Minister

687
00:57:01.000 --> 00:57:03.000
sacking you was
a grave misstep.

688
00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:05.000
Flattery will get you
everywhere.

689
00:57:05.000 --> 00:57:07.000
How can I help you?

690
00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:11.000
Does the name Michael Mason
ring any bells?

691
00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:16.000
Where did you hear that name?

692
00:57:16.000 --> 00:57:19.000
He took down a full
assault team...

693
00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:21.000
alone.

694
00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:25.000
What I'm about to say
doesn't exist

695
00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:28.000
outside of this conversation.

696
00:57:29.000 --> 00:57:32.000
Years ago,
we ran an off-book program

697
00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:35.000
of elite operatives
called Black Kites.

698
00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:39.000
Operatives untethered
from MI6's oversight.

699
00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:41.000
And Mason was one of them.

700
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:43.000
Yeah. He was one of the first.

701
00:57:43.000 --> 00:57:49.000
He was a prodigy.
He became our gold standard.

702
00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:50.000
Then what happened?

703
00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:52.000
He was sent to eliminate

704
00:57:52.000 --> 00:57:53.000
a foreign intelligence officer.

705
00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:55.000
Instead, he spared the target,

706
00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:58.000
falsified his report,
and then disappeared.

707
00:57:58.000 --> 00:58:01.000
Why would he defy orders?

708
00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:03.000
We think he was turned.

709
00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:06.000
I'm sure for a king's ransom.

710
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:09.000
You need to understand
something.

711
00:58:09.000 --> 00:58:11.000
[suspenseful music]

712
00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:13.000
Mason isn't just an assassin.

713
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:16.000
He's a precision instrument.

714
00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:18.000
There's no stopping him.

715
00:58:18.000 --> 00:58:22.000
You need to throw everything
you've got at him, Roberta.

716
00:58:22.000 --> 00:58:24.000
Michael Mason unfortunately

717
00:58:24.000 --> 00:58:29.000
has become a cancer
on all that we stand for.

718
00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:33.000
Yes, sir.

719
00:58:33.000 --> 00:58:36.000
[sinister music continues]

720
00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:43.000
[sighs]

721
00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:52.000
Ready to put your trade craft
to the test?

722
00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:57.000
Am I gonna get fired for this?

723
00:58:57.000 --> 00:59:00.000
Not unless I do.

724
00:59:02.000 --> 00:59:06.000
I found the Black Kite files
on a backup server.

725
00:59:06.000 --> 00:59:09.000
Mason was helping
an Iranian scientist defect

726
00:59:09.000 --> 00:59:12.000
after he gave us everything
on their nuclear program.

727
00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:14.000
Instead of protecting him,

728
00:59:14.000 --> 00:59:18.000
Mason was ordered to kill him
for deniability.

729
00:59:18.000 --> 00:59:20.000
It looks like he refused.

730
00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:22.000
[suspenseful music]

731
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:25.000
Good girl, Maddie.

732
00:59:28.000 --> 00:59:30.000
[sinister music fades in]

733
00:59:32.000 --> 00:59:35.000
Damn it, Roberta.

734
00:59:35.000 --> 00:59:38.000
Some people just can't
help themselves.

735
00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:45.000
[car humming gently]

736
00:59:54.000 --> 00:59:56.000
You okay?

737
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.000
You think I can't handle
the truth

738
01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:05.000
about who you really are,
but I can.

739
01:00:17.000 --> 01:00:21.000
Well... do you have family
somewhere?

740
01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:27.000
No.

741
01:00:28.000 --> 01:00:31.000
You never wanted one?

742
01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:34.000
A wife, kids?

743
01:00:38.000 --> 01:00:41.000
[sighs] It complicates things.

744
01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:49.000
I'd rather it be complicated,
then.

745
01:00:50.000 --> 01:00:52.000
And have my mum back.

746
01:00:53.000 --> 01:00:55.000
My uncle too.

747
01:00:55.000 --> 01:00:58.000
Now I have no one.

748
01:00:58.000 --> 01:01:00.000
[poignant music]

749
01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:04.000
I wish I could tell you
life would always be fair.

750
01:01:04.000 --> 01:01:07.000
But you already know the truth
to that.

751
01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:13.000
No kid should have to go through
what you did.

752
01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:20.000
Just don't ever let it break
your spirit.

753
01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:22.000
No matter what.

754
01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:25.000
Okay?

755
01:01:39.000 --> 01:01:43.000
[paper crumpling, unfolding]

756
01:01:49.000 --> 01:01:51.000
Here.

757
01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:55.000
At least you had Jack.

758
01:01:55.000 --> 01:01:58.000
He was your family.

759
01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:04.000
Better you keep it.

760
01:02:12.000 --> 01:02:14.000
[church bell ringing]

761
01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:34.000
Okay, there's a camera up
on the wall in front of us.

762
01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:36.000
There's also one behind us.

763
01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:38.000
I want you to get out
on my side,

764
01:02:38.000 --> 01:02:41.000
keep your head down
and keep it forward.

765
01:02:55.000 --> 01:02:57.000
[suspenseful music]

766
01:02:57.000 --> 01:03:00.000
[system beeping]

767
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:17.000
[sighs]

768
01:03:17.000 --> 01:03:20.000
[keyboard tapping]

769
01:03:20.000 --> 01:03:22.000
[phone beeping]

770
01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:36.000
[birds singing]

771
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:44.000
[sinister music]

772
01:03:59.000 --> 01:04:02.000
So, when did you find religion?

773
01:04:02.000 --> 01:04:04.000
Today...

774
01:04:04.000 --> 01:04:06.000
when a ghost called me.

775
01:04:09.000 --> 01:04:11.000
Oh, we have different
interpretations

776
01:04:11.000 --> 01:04:14.000
of what "baggage" means.

777
01:04:14.000 --> 01:04:16.000
Just saying.

778
01:04:16.000 --> 01:04:18.000
[car engine roaring]

779
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:22.000
[light music playing on radio]

780
01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:43.000
[birds singing]

781
01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:01.000
[keys jangling]

782
01:05:07.000 --> 01:05:10.000
Uh, no, that's the workshop.
Um...

783
01:05:10.000 --> 01:05:13.000
I'm always building
one thing or another.

784
01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:17.000
Just be careful, though,
there's lots of tools about.

785
01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:22.000
Uh, Jessie?

786
01:05:22.000 --> 01:05:24.000
Why don't you go get a drink?

787
01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:26.000
The kitchen's in the back.

788
01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:28.000
If you want me to leave
so you guys can talk,

789
01:05:28.000 --> 01:05:30.000
you can just say that.

790
01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:32.000
[footsteps receding]

791
01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:35.000
Hey, hey...

792
01:05:36.000 --> 01:05:38.000
It's okay.

793
01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:46.000
Spirited girl.

794
01:05:48.000 --> 01:05:50.000
Who is she?
What are you doing here?

795
01:05:50.000 --> 01:05:54.000
Her uncle and I,
we served together.

796
01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:57.000
I need a way out... for her.

797
01:05:58.000 --> 01:06:01.000
Then I'll start figuring out
how they found me.

798
01:06:01.000 --> 01:06:04.000
Don't tell me you've got
sentimental in your old age?

799
01:06:04.000 --> 01:06:05.000
- [suspenseful music]
- She's just a kid

800
01:06:05.000 --> 01:06:08.000
who was in the wrong place
at the wrong time.

801
01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:10.000
Christ, Mason...

802
01:06:46.000 --> 01:06:48.000
[pills rattle]

803
01:06:54.000 --> 01:06:57.000
[keyboard clacking]

804
01:06:57.000 --> 01:06:59.000
Meet THEA.

805
01:06:59.000 --> 01:07:02.000
I helped build it
before I left the circus.

806
01:07:02.000 --> 01:07:04.000
The big question is...

807
01:07:04.000 --> 01:07:07.000
how the hell did they find you
after I buried you?

808
01:07:07.000 --> 01:07:10.000
[sinister music]

809
01:07:10.000 --> 01:07:13.000
Shit.

810
01:07:20.000 --> 01:07:22.000
When it was time for you
to disappear, I...

811
01:07:22.000 --> 01:07:26.000
I changed your identity
to an oil worker in Aberdeen.

812
01:07:26.000 --> 01:07:28.000
A nobody.
But someone figured it out,

813
01:07:28.000 --> 01:07:31.000
and swapped it to this guy.

814
01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:33.000
A high-value terrorist
on the watch list.

815
01:07:33.000 --> 01:07:37.000
Which you know carries
an interagency kill order.

816
01:07:40.000 --> 01:07:41.000
Manafort.

817
01:07:41.000 --> 01:07:43.000
You... you really think
he still wants you dead

818
01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:46.000
after all this time?

819
01:07:46.000 --> 01:07:48.000
I broke the only rule
that matters to him.

820
01:07:48.000 --> 01:07:49.000
Fuck his rules.

821
01:07:49.000 --> 01:07:51.000
You refused to kill
an innocent man,

822
01:07:51.000 --> 01:07:55.000
that you promised to help
after he helped us.

823
01:07:55.000 --> 01:07:56.000
Can you shut it down?

824
01:07:56.000 --> 01:07:59.000
Not from here.

825
01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:04.000
I mean, it wouldn't matter
anyway. You've been ID'd.

826
01:08:04.000 --> 01:08:06.000
All those years on that island.

827
01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:08.000
You should have stayed dead,
Mason.

828
01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:11.000
Yeah, that's my problem.

829
01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:14.000
I just need you to keep
Jessie safe.

830
01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:17.000
Manafort knows who she is now...

831
01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:20.000
which makes her a loose end.

832
01:08:21.000 --> 01:08:23.000
You care about her, don't you?

833
01:08:26.000 --> 01:08:29.000
This is where we part ways.

834
01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:33.000
Can you keep her here?

835
01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:37.000
Look, Mason, I... I can't.

836
01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:40.000
Why?

837
01:08:41.000 --> 01:08:44.000
He has cancer.

838
01:08:46.000 --> 01:08:48.000
My mum took the same meds
before she...

839
01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:53.000
[poignant music]

840
01:08:55.000 --> 01:08:58.000
I'm sorry I'm such a drag
to you.

841
01:08:58.000 --> 01:09:00.000
Hey, Jessie, wait.

842
01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:03.000
[dark music]

843
01:09:04.000 --> 01:09:06.000
Is she right?

844
01:09:08.000 --> 01:09:11.000
Doctors say I might get
one more Christmas.

845
01:09:11.000 --> 01:09:14.000
Oh, Jesus.

846
01:09:14.000 --> 01:09:17.000
I'd help you if I could.

847
01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:19.000
But you know I can't be
responsible for her.

848
01:09:19.000 --> 01:09:22.000
My hands are tied.

849
01:09:25.000 --> 01:09:28.000
What if I go to Kamal?

850
01:09:29.000 --> 01:09:31.000
He has the means
to get her out...

851
01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:33.000
- undetected.
- Kamal Shah?

852
01:09:33.000 --> 01:09:36.000
- [sinister music]
- No. No, no, no way.

853
01:09:36.000 --> 01:09:37.000
- Not an option!
- Hey, look.

854
01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:39.000
He's the best at what he does.

855
01:09:39.000 --> 01:09:41.000
Yeah, because
he's a violent trafficker.

856
01:09:41.000 --> 01:09:44.000
And you haven't got MI6
behind you to control him now.

857
01:09:44.000 --> 01:09:47.000
Let me worry about that.

858
01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:49.000
Just help me get to him.

859
01:09:50.000 --> 01:09:52.000
Can you do that?

860
01:09:54.000 --> 01:09:59.000
Listen, I... I can tell you
when to turn left or right.

861
01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:02.000
That's about it.

862
01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:05.000
Good enough.

863
01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:07.000
[birds twittering]

864
01:10:45.000 --> 01:10:49.000
Hey, Jessie. It's time to go.

865
01:10:52.000 --> 01:10:55.000
Hey, Jessie, come on.

866
01:10:57.000 --> 01:11:00.000
Were you really gonna
leave me here?

867
01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:02.000
I'm sorry.

868
01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:07.000
Your safety is the most
important thing to me.

869
01:11:09.000 --> 01:11:11.000
Please.

870
01:11:13.000 --> 01:11:15.000
Fine.

871
01:11:18.000 --> 01:11:20.000
[clattering]

872
01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:24.000
- [quietly] Go stand by the wall.
- But...

873
01:11:24.000 --> 01:11:27.000
Just do it!
[whispers] Stand by the wall.

874
01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:30.000
[ominous music]

875
01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:34.000
[fire poker clinks]

876
01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:38.000
[door creaks]

877
01:11:48.000 --> 01:11:51.000
[ominous music intensifies]

878
01:12:03.000 --> 01:12:05.000
[clock ticking]

879
01:12:05.000 --> 01:12:08.000
[suspenseful music fades in]

880
01:12:10.000 --> 01:12:13.000
[rapid gunfire]

881
01:12:13.000 --> 01:12:14.000
[yelps]

882
01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:15.000
Jesus!

883
01:12:15.000 --> 01:12:17.000
- [gunfire continues]
- Hurgh!

884
01:12:17.000 --> 01:12:19.000
- [crashing]
- Aaargh!

885
01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:22.000
- Urgh!
- Argh!

886
01:12:22.000 --> 01:12:24.000
- [blow lands]
- Ooh!

887
01:12:24.000 --> 01:12:26.000
- [grunting]
- [smashing]

888
01:12:26.000 --> 01:12:28.000
[grunting]

889
01:12:28.000 --> 01:12:31.000
[ominous music]

890
01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:34.000
Argh!

891
01:12:34.000 --> 01:12:37.000
[grunting continues]

892
01:12:37.000 --> 01:12:40.000
[crashing]

893
01:12:48.000 --> 01:12:50.000
[grunting]

894
01:12:50.000 --> 01:12:52.000
[breathing heavily]

895
01:12:59.000 --> 01:13:02.000
[blade clicks]

896
01:13:09.000 --> 01:13:11.000
- [suspenseful music]
- [grunting resumes]

897
01:13:22.000 --> 01:13:24.000
[shattering]

898
01:13:36.000 --> 01:13:39.000
[suspenseful music continues]

899
01:13:40.000 --> 01:13:42.000
[grunting]

900
01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:44.000
[gunshot]

901
01:13:44.000 --> 01:13:46.000
[ominous music]

902
01:13:46.000 --> 01:13:48.000
Let him go.

903
01:13:50.000 --> 01:13:52.000
[tearful] Just let him go.

904
01:13:52.000 --> 01:13:54.000
- Argh!
- [thud]

905
01:13:54.000 --> 01:13:56.000
- [grappling]
- [Jessie screams]

906
01:13:57.000 --> 01:13:59.000
[nail gun shots]

907
01:13:59.000 --> 01:14:01.000
Come on!

908
01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:05.000
[gunfire]

909
01:14:05.000 --> 01:14:07.000
[smashing]

910
01:14:07.000 --> 01:14:11.000
Get here in now, go!
Go, go, get in!

911
01:14:12.000 --> 01:14:14.000
- [car doors slam]
- [engine revs]

912
01:14:14.000 --> 01:14:16.000
[grunts, smashes]

913
01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:18.000
[high-tempo music]

914
01:14:19.000 --> 01:14:22.000
[gunfire]

915
01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:31.000
Jesus!

916
01:14:31.000 --> 01:14:33.000
Who was that?

917
01:14:33.000 --> 01:14:34.000
Him.

918
01:14:34.000 --> 01:14:37.000
20 years ago.

919
01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:42.000
[panting]

920
01:14:42.000 --> 01:14:44.000
[phone beeps]

921
01:14:45.000 --> 01:14:48.000
[suspenseful music]

922
01:15:02.000 --> 01:15:04.000
Ross?

923
01:15:05.000 --> 01:15:07.000
We're doubling down,
get your team ready.

924
01:15:07.000 --> 01:15:09.000
Yes, sir.

925
01:15:16.000 --> 01:15:19.000
Booth: The Wi-Fi in there
will suffice for my needs.

926
01:15:19.000 --> 01:15:21.000
Here, take my hat and coat.

927
01:15:21.000 --> 01:15:23.000
Help you hide those good looks.

928
01:15:23.000 --> 01:15:25.000
Right.

929
01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:27.000
Use only for an emergency,

930
01:15:27.000 --> 01:15:31.000
or you know they'll trace you
in a heartbeat.

931
01:15:31.000 --> 01:15:33.000
Yeah, we're gonna
have to switch motors.

932
01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:36.000
They know we're in this one now.

933
01:15:37.000 --> 01:15:39.000
[poignant music]

934
01:15:39.000 --> 01:15:42.000
You take care, young lady.

935
01:15:42.000 --> 01:15:43.000
Thank you.

936
01:15:43.000 --> 01:15:46.000
[dramatic music]

937
01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:03.000
I wish you'd killed that man.

938
01:16:05.000 --> 01:16:08.000
I know it's wrong to say that,
but...

939
01:16:11.000 --> 01:16:14.000
Maybe I'm becoming like you.

940
01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:18.000
You're nothing like me, Jessie.

941
01:16:18.000 --> 01:16:21.000
And I'm keeping it that way.

942
01:16:21.000 --> 01:16:23.000
But how do you know?

943
01:16:23.000 --> 01:16:25.000
[chuckles]

944
01:16:26.000 --> 01:16:29.000
Because I've seen
who you really are.

945
01:16:32.000 --> 01:16:36.000
Look... by tonight, all of this
will be behind you.

946
01:16:36.000 --> 01:16:39.000
You'll start a brand-new life...

947
01:16:39.000 --> 01:16:42.000
somewhere normal,
somewhere safe.

948
01:16:42.000 --> 01:16:45.000
And alone.

949
01:16:45.000 --> 01:16:48.000
[dark music]

950
01:16:48.000 --> 01:16:50.000
What will you do?

951
01:16:51.000 --> 01:16:54.000
You can't go back
to your island.

952
01:16:54.000 --> 01:16:57.000
There's always another island.

953
01:17:06.000 --> 01:17:08.000
I could come with you.

954
01:17:12.000 --> 01:17:14.000
You don't want this life.

955
01:17:14.000 --> 01:17:17.000
Always on the run,
looking over your shoulder...

956
01:17:17.000 --> 01:17:18.000
And you do?

957
01:17:18.000 --> 01:17:21.000
Hey, Jessie,
you need to understand.

958
01:17:21.000 --> 01:17:24.000
The only way that I can
protect you...

959
01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:27.000
is to stop the people
that are doing this.

960
01:17:29.000 --> 01:17:32.000
[exhales]

961
01:17:35.000 --> 01:17:38.000
[exhales]

962
01:17:47.000 --> 01:17:50.000
[suspenseful music]

963
01:17:51.000 --> 01:17:53.000
[sirens wailing]

964
01:17:59.000 --> 01:18:02.000
[people shouting]

965
01:18:04.000 --> 01:18:06.000
[suspenseful music continues]

966
01:18:28.000 --> 01:18:31.000
You need to stay close to me,
all right?

967
01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:36.000
[suspenseful music resumes]

968
01:18:41.000 --> 01:18:44.000
[train clattering distantly]

969
01:18:48.000 --> 01:18:52.000
[siren wailing
in background]

970
01:18:53.000 --> 01:18:55.000
Any sign of Mason?

971
01:18:55.000 --> 01:18:57.000
No. We have nothing.

972
01:18:57.000 --> 01:19:00.000
[sighs] He knows what
he's doing.

973
01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:02.000
You're right.

974
01:19:02.000 --> 01:19:06.000
I found an unknown login to
THEA from outside MI6.

975
01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:08.000
Roberta: I have
a bad feeling.

976
01:19:08.000 --> 01:19:09.000
Can you ID?

977
01:19:09.000 --> 01:19:11.000
No.

978
01:19:11.000 --> 01:19:15.000
There is...
there is something I can try.

979
01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:17.000
Whatever it is,
do it quickly.

980
01:19:17.000 --> 01:19:18.000
[taps keyboard,
computer bleeps]

981
01:19:18.000 --> 01:19:21.000
- [keyboard clacking]
- [high-tempo music]

982
01:19:21.000 --> 01:19:23.000
[train clattering]

983
01:19:24.000 --> 01:19:27.000
[distant chatter]

984
01:19:27.000 --> 01:19:30.000
[sinister music]

985
01:19:34.000 --> 01:19:37.000
There's a camera.
It'll see us.

986
01:19:37.000 --> 01:19:40.000
Let's hope it's working.

987
01:19:43.000 --> 01:19:45.000
Sorry, mate. Invite only.

988
01:19:45.000 --> 01:19:47.000
- [blow lands]
- [groans]

989
01:19:47.000 --> 01:19:49.000
- [grunting]
- [blows continue]

990
01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:50.000
Aargh!

991
01:19:50.000 --> 01:19:52.000
Take me to Kamal,

992
01:19:52.000 --> 01:19:53.000
or I'll break your
other wrist.

993
01:19:53.000 --> 01:19:56.000
[high-tempo music]

994
01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:03.000
[bleeping]

995
01:20:04.000 --> 01:20:07.000
[tapping furiously
on keyboard]

996
01:20:09.000 --> 01:20:11.000
[sighs]

997
01:20:11.000 --> 01:20:13.000
Well played, Roberta.

998
01:20:13.000 --> 01:20:16.000
My trap worked. I got him.

999
01:20:17.000 --> 01:20:19.000
It's...

1000
01:20:20.000 --> 01:20:22.000
Oh, shit.

1001
01:20:22.000 --> 01:20:24.000
- That's...
- Stephen Manafort.

1002
01:20:24.000 --> 01:20:26.000
[sinister music]

1003
01:20:27.000 --> 01:20:30.000
I know.
We'll deal with him later.

1004
01:20:31.000 --> 01:20:35.000
Get me every camera
in this club, now!

1005
01:20:35.000 --> 01:20:38.000
[club music thumping]

1006
01:20:46.000 --> 01:20:49.000
Let's keep this walk
nice and smooth.

1007
01:21:10.000 --> 01:21:12.000
[music volume increases]

1008
01:21:25.000 --> 01:21:28.000
Tell him it's Michael Mason.

1009
01:21:45.000 --> 01:21:48.000
Do you know Michael
Mason, boss?

1010
01:22:10.000 --> 01:22:12.000
Michael Mason.

1011
01:22:12.000 --> 01:22:14.000
Look at you.

1012
01:22:15.000 --> 01:22:18.000
No country, no badge.

1013
01:22:18.000 --> 01:22:23.000
Just a poor bastard who
thought he had friends in the game.

1014
01:22:25.000 --> 01:22:27.000
Who's she?

1015
01:22:28.000 --> 01:22:29.000
I need a way out...

1016
01:22:29.000 --> 01:22:33.000
of the country for
her. Tonight.

1017
01:22:33.000 --> 01:22:37.000
New identity.
Somewhere off grid.

1018
01:22:37.000 --> 01:22:38.000
No.

1019
01:22:38.000 --> 01:22:40.000
No?

1020
01:22:40.000 --> 01:22:41.000
How do you think you've been
allowed to operate

1021
01:22:41.000 --> 01:22:45.000
for all these years, Kamal?
With impunity.

1022
01:22:45.000 --> 01:22:48.000
And with the luxury of
getting rid of your competition

1023
01:22:48.000 --> 01:22:50.000
at the same time.

1024
01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:54.000
By ratting them out to
Manafort and I.

1025
01:22:55.000 --> 01:22:57.000
Manafort's gone.

1026
01:22:57.000 --> 01:22:59.000
Not gone...

1027
01:22:59.000 --> 01:23:00.000
unshackled.

1028
01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:04.000
He's more dangerous than
ever to us both.

1029
01:23:05.000 --> 01:23:07.000
- You're lying.
- Am I?

1030
01:23:07.000 --> 01:23:10.000
The second the security
camera outside saw me walk in here,

1031
01:23:10.000 --> 01:23:15.000
into your club, every
operative MI6 has within 25 miles

1032
01:23:15.000 --> 01:23:18.000
was activated to
bring me in.

1033
01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:22.000
I reckon
you've got ten minutes, tops.

1034
01:23:22.000 --> 01:23:24.000
All I need is for you
to get her out.

1035
01:23:24.000 --> 01:23:27.000
And I'll go cut the head
off the snake.

1036
01:23:27.000 --> 01:23:30.000
Bury all our dirty little
secrets with him.

1037
01:23:34.000 --> 01:23:36.000
Wait here.

1038
01:23:36.000 --> 01:23:39.000
[club music continues]

1039
01:23:39.000 --> 01:23:42.000
[music thumping distantly]

1040
01:23:44.000 --> 01:23:47.000
[door closes]

1041
01:23:48.000 --> 01:23:51.000
[sinister music fades in]

1042
01:23:52.000 --> 01:23:55.000
Please come with me.

1043
01:23:55.000 --> 01:23:58.000
You heard the deal
I made with him.

1044
01:23:59.000 --> 01:24:01.000
I need to honor my side.

1045
01:24:01.000 --> 01:24:03.000
Honor your side?

1046
01:24:06.000 --> 01:24:08.000
I think you wanna die.

1047
01:24:08.000 --> 01:24:10.000
What's that supposed
to mean?

1048
01:24:10.000 --> 01:24:13.000
You don't think you have
anything to live for.

1049
01:24:15.000 --> 01:24:17.000
If you really wanted to,
you'd come!

1050
01:24:17.000 --> 01:24:21.000
Hey, people like me don't
get to go and live a normal life!

1051
01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:24.000
You keep telling
yourself that.

1052
01:24:31.000 --> 01:24:33.000
[whispers] Hey, hey...

1053
01:24:33.000 --> 01:24:36.000
- You're stronger than this.
- No, I'm not.

1054
01:24:36.000 --> 01:24:38.000
Yes, you are.

1055
01:24:39.000 --> 01:24:41.000
I need you to be.

1056
01:24:42.000 --> 01:24:45.000
Just promise me you're not
going to die?

1057
01:24:50.000 --> 01:24:52.000
Exactly.

1058
01:24:59.000 --> 01:25:01.000
Roberta: Right,
where's my tactical team?

1059
01:25:01.000 --> 01:25:03.000
- En route.
- I want Mason and the girl

1060
01:25:03.000 --> 01:25:07.000
taken in alive.
They are not to open fire.

1061
01:25:07.000 --> 01:25:09.000
- [sinister music]
- Car's out front.

1062
01:25:09.000 --> 01:25:10.000
How far out is your team?

1063
01:25:10.000 --> 01:25:13.000
They're still en route, sir.

1064
01:25:13.000 --> 01:25:15.000
Where the fuck are you?

1065
01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:16.000
[van roaring]

1066
01:25:16.000 --> 01:25:18.000
Thirty seconds out, sir.

1067
01:25:18.000 --> 01:25:19.000
The girl
is his Achilles' heel.

1068
01:25:19.000 --> 01:25:21.000
Use that to your advantage.

1069
01:25:21.000 --> 01:25:23.000
Copy that, sir.

1070
01:25:23.000 --> 01:25:25.000
[guns loading]

1071
01:25:25.000 --> 01:25:28.000
[door opens]

1072
01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:33.000
Passport, ID and
20,000 euros.

1073
01:25:33.000 --> 01:25:36.000
She goes to our safe house
in Spain for now.

1074
01:25:37.000 --> 01:25:41.000
Boat leaves Isle of Dogs
in 30 minutes. It won't wait.

1075
01:25:41.000 --> 01:25:44.000
Just make sure you finish
what you started.

1076
01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:48.000
If you handle your end,
I'll handle mine.

1077
01:25:48.000 --> 01:25:50.000
[zipping]

1078
01:25:53.000 --> 01:25:56.000
[tires squealing]

1079
01:25:59.000 --> 01:26:01.000
Wait on the other side
of the square.

1080
01:26:01.000 --> 01:26:04.000
Let's move. All
right, let's go.

1081
01:26:04.000 --> 01:26:07.000
[people chattering happily]

1082
01:26:09.000 --> 01:26:10.000
This is Zulu, two
minutes out.

1083
01:26:10.000 --> 01:26:12.000
Do we have
an exact location inside?

1084
01:26:12.000 --> 01:26:13.000
Aziz: Wait,
you're not already there?

1085
01:26:13.000 --> 01:26:15.000
That's a negative.

1086
01:26:15.000 --> 01:26:18.000
[high-tempo music continues]

1087
01:26:18.000 --> 01:26:21.000
Manafort. Tell them that
there's a rogue team already inside.

1088
01:26:21.000 --> 01:26:24.000
They need to get in
there now! Now!

1089
01:26:24.000 --> 01:26:26.000
[club music thumping]

1090
01:26:55.000 --> 01:26:57.000
[man cries out in pain]

1091
01:26:57.000 --> 01:26:59.000
- [grunting]
- Argh!

1092
01:26:59.000 --> 01:27:02.000
[clubbers cheering]

1093
01:27:17.000 --> 01:27:20.000
[club music continues]

1094
01:27:41.000 --> 01:27:43.000
[people screaming]

1095
01:27:43.000 --> 01:27:46.000
It's okay.

1096
01:27:49.000 --> 01:27:50.000
- [silenced gunshots]
- Argh!

1097
01:27:50.000 --> 01:27:52.000
[woman screams]

1098
01:27:52.000 --> 01:27:56.000
[chaotic shouting]

1099
01:27:59.000 --> 01:28:02.000
[club music thumping]

1100
01:28:13.000 --> 01:28:15.000
[people chattering]

1101
01:28:21.000 --> 01:28:24.000
- [screams]
- [gunfire]

1102
01:28:25.000 --> 01:28:29.000
[shouting and gunfire
continues]

1103
01:28:31.000 --> 01:28:33.000
[screaming]

1104
01:28:35.000 --> 01:28:39.000
- [grunting]
- [gunshots]

1105
01:28:48.000 --> 01:28:51.000
[club music thumping]

1106
01:28:54.000 --> 01:28:57.000
[struggling]

1107
01:28:58.000 --> 01:29:00.000
Argh!

1108
01:29:03.000 --> 01:29:06.000
[Jessie grunting]

1109
01:29:07.000 --> 01:29:10.000
- [gunshot]
- [woman screams]

1110
01:29:10.000 --> 01:29:13.000
- [gunshot]
- [people screaming]

1111
01:29:14.000 --> 01:29:17.000
[gunfire continues]

1112
01:29:17.000 --> 01:29:19.000
[glass smashing]

1113
01:29:19.000 --> 01:29:22.000
Get out of here!
Move out of the way!

1114
01:29:22.000 --> 01:29:23.000
[screaming]

1115
01:29:23.000 --> 01:29:27.000
Mason!

1116
01:29:27.000 --> 01:29:30.000
- [loud bang]
- [alarm blares]

1117
01:29:34.000 --> 01:29:38.000
Arthur. Manafort's guards
have got Jessie.

1118
01:29:38.000 --> 01:29:41.000
Move, move, move.
Out of the way! Out the way!

1119
01:29:41.000 --> 01:29:44.000
Found her. Hold on.

1120
01:29:44.000 --> 01:29:46.000
Out the front entrance.

1121
01:29:46.000 --> 01:29:47.000
Cut across the square
and turn south.

1122
01:29:47.000 --> 01:29:51.000
She's being carried
towards a black transit van.

1123
01:29:51.000 --> 01:29:52.000
Open it up!

1124
01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:56.000
- I've got her! Move, move!
- Help me!

1125
01:29:56.000 --> 01:29:57.000
- Go, go, go!
- [Jessie screaming]

1126
01:29:57.000 --> 01:29:58.000
Get ready!

1127
01:29:58.000 --> 01:30:01.000
He's gonna be coming
for her!

1128
01:30:01.000 --> 01:30:02.000
Get in there!

1129
01:30:02.000 --> 01:30:04.000
[struggling]

1130
01:30:04.000 --> 01:30:06.000
Where are you going?
Get in there!

1131
01:30:06.000 --> 01:30:09.000
[Jessie panting]

1132
01:30:09.000 --> 01:30:13.000
[clubbers screaming]

1133
01:30:13.000 --> 01:30:15.000
I don't see Mason.

1134
01:30:15.000 --> 01:30:16.000
There!

1135
01:30:16.000 --> 01:30:18.000
[clubbers screaming]

1136
01:30:18.000 --> 01:30:21.000
[dramatic music]

1137
01:30:21.000 --> 01:30:24.000
Mason's heading
right towards you.

1138
01:30:25.000 --> 01:30:27.000
[car screeches]

1139
01:30:27.000 --> 01:30:30.000
[commandos shouting]

1140
01:30:33.000 --> 01:30:35.000
[people whimpering]

1141
01:30:35.000 --> 01:30:36.000
- [gunshot]
- [screaming]

1142
01:30:36.000 --> 01:30:37.000
Move!

1143
01:30:37.000 --> 01:30:40.000
[struggling]

1144
01:30:40.000 --> 01:30:41.000
[gunshot]

1145
01:30:41.000 --> 01:30:44.000
- [blows landing]
- [grunting]

1146
01:30:44.000 --> 01:30:46.000
[crying]

1147
01:30:46.000 --> 01:30:48.000
[screaming]

1148
01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:50.000
Move!

1149
01:30:50.000 --> 01:30:52.000
Fucking move.

1150
01:31:03.000 --> 01:31:05.000
[gunshots echo]

1151
01:31:05.000 --> 01:31:07.000
[panicking]

1152
01:31:07.000 --> 01:31:10.000
[sirens blaring]

1153
01:31:11.000 --> 01:31:14.000
[sinister music]

1154
01:31:18.000 --> 01:31:20.000
I got you.

1155
01:31:20.000 --> 01:31:22.000
It's okay.

1156
01:31:23.000 --> 01:31:25.000
I got you.

1157
01:31:25.000 --> 01:31:27.000
I got you, Jessie.

1158
01:31:27.000 --> 01:31:29.000
[exhales]

1159
01:31:29.000 --> 01:31:31.000
I got you.

1160
01:31:36.000 --> 01:31:38.000
You okay?

1161
01:31:38.000 --> 01:31:40.000
- [suspenseful music]
- Time to go.

1162
01:31:45.000 --> 01:31:47.000
[engine starts]

1163
01:31:50.000 --> 01:31:53.000
[police siren wailing]

1164
01:31:58.000 --> 01:32:01.000
[dramatic music fades in]

1165
01:32:34.000 --> 01:32:37.000
[dramatic music continues]

1166
01:32:40.000 --> 01:32:42.000
There's your ride.

1167
01:33:01.000 --> 01:33:03.000
Hey.

1168
01:33:03.000 --> 01:33:05.000
You're gonna be okay.

1169
01:33:07.000 --> 01:33:09.000
Come on.

1170
01:33:14.000 --> 01:33:16.000
Come on.

1171
01:33:16.000 --> 01:33:18.000
Gonna lower her down.

1172
01:33:18.000 --> 01:33:20.000
Man: You've gotta hurry!

1173
01:33:21.000 --> 01:33:23.000
- Ready? It's time to go.
- [upset] No.

1174
01:33:23.000 --> 01:33:27.000
- The boat won't wait.
- No, no, no. You...

1175
01:33:27.000 --> 01:33:30.000
You said you can't live
a normal life, but you're wrong.

1176
01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:32.000
You just have to come
on the boat with me

1177
01:33:32.000 --> 01:33:33.000
and we can... we
can disappear

1178
01:33:33.000 --> 01:33:35.000
and we can have
a normal life.

1179
01:33:35.000 --> 01:33:37.000
- Come on.
- Please. No, please!

1180
01:33:37.000 --> 01:33:38.000
- Please!
- The boat won't wait.

1181
01:33:38.000 --> 01:33:41.000
You're all I have now!

1182
01:33:43.000 --> 01:33:46.000
I don't wanna leave you.

1183
01:33:47.000 --> 01:33:49.000
Hey. Jessie.

1184
01:33:49.000 --> 01:33:51.000
- No!
- Listen to me.

1185
01:33:51.000 --> 01:33:53.000
[sobs]

1186
01:33:53.000 --> 01:33:55.000
- Jessie.
- No!

1187
01:33:55.000 --> 01:33:59.000
This is the only way
I can keep you safe.

1188
01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:01.000
I'm sorry.

1189
01:34:01.000 --> 01:34:05.000
No! I'm not...
I'm not leaving without you!

1190
01:34:05.000 --> 01:34:07.000
[poignant music]

1191
01:34:08.000 --> 01:34:11.000
I have to save you!

1192
01:34:12.000 --> 01:34:15.000
You saved me already.

1193
01:34:17.000 --> 01:34:20.000
You saved me already.

1194
01:34:21.000 --> 01:34:23.000
- Come on.
- [gunshot]

1195
01:34:23.000 --> 01:34:24.000
[Jessie screams]

1196
01:34:24.000 --> 01:34:27.000
- Now, Jessie!
- No!

1197
01:34:27.000 --> 01:34:30.000
- [yelps]
- Okay, she's safe.

1198
01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:31.000
[boat engine roars]

1199
01:34:31.000 --> 01:34:33.000
No, no, please!

1200
01:34:33.000 --> 01:34:36.000
[sobs]

1201
01:34:37.000 --> 01:34:39.000
[gunshots echo]

1202
01:34:39.000 --> 01:34:42.000
[dramatic music]

1203
01:35:05.000 --> 01:35:09.000
[gunshots echo distantly]

1204
01:35:13.000 --> 01:35:16.000
[boat motor roaring]

1205
01:35:21.000 --> 01:35:23.000
Do you even know why
you're doing this?

1206
01:35:26.000 --> 01:35:28.000
Does it matter?

1207
01:35:29.000 --> 01:35:31.000
You can't save her either.

1208
01:35:31.000 --> 01:35:34.000
- [blows landing]
- [grunting]

1209
01:35:37.000 --> 01:35:40.000
[loud thud]

1210
01:35:47.000 --> 01:35:50.000
- [ominous music]
- [grunts]

1211
01:35:52.000 --> 01:35:54.000
[clanking]

1212
01:35:56.000 --> 01:35:59.000
[grunting, groaning]

1213
01:35:59.000 --> 01:36:02.000
[grunting]

1214
01:36:08.000 --> 01:36:11.000
[dramatic music fades in]

1215
01:36:13.000 --> 01:36:16.000
[both grunting]

1216
01:36:19.000 --> 01:36:22.000
- [grunting continues]
- Argh!

1217
01:36:29.000 --> 01:36:32.000
[breathing heavily]

1218
01:36:32.000 --> 01:36:35.000
[clanking]

1219
01:36:37.000 --> 01:36:39.000
[thump]

1220
01:36:39.000 --> 01:36:42.000
[sinister music]

1221
01:36:52.000 --> 01:36:54.000
[chain rattles]

1222
01:37:03.000 --> 01:37:05.000
Newly appointed MI6 head,
Roberta Frost,

1223
01:37:05.000 --> 01:37:08.000
is dealing with
the fallout...

1224
01:37:09.000 --> 01:37:12.000
[gentle music playing]

1225
01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:24.000
[drink pouring]

1226
01:37:31.000 --> 01:37:33.000
[sighs]

1227
01:37:40.000 --> 01:37:42.000
[sniffs]

1228
01:37:47.000 --> 01:37:50.000
You were my dearest...

1229
01:37:51.000 --> 01:37:54.000
my greatest weapon.

1230
01:37:55.000 --> 01:37:58.000
And then you broke
the rules.

1231
01:37:59.000 --> 01:38:05.000
Black Kites know one law
above all: loyalty.

1232
01:38:05.000 --> 01:38:10.000
You put your conscience
first and the mission second.

1233
01:38:10.000 --> 01:38:13.000
I finally put humanity
over blind obedience.

1234
01:38:13.000 --> 01:38:16.000
Oh, yeah. There it is.
The righteous martyr.

1235
01:38:16.000 --> 01:38:19.000
And a foolish one. You
allowed a civilian into this game.

1236
01:38:19.000 --> 01:38:22.000
A child! What good is
all that humanity

1237
01:38:22.000 --> 01:38:25.000
with her blood
on your hands?

1238
01:38:25.000 --> 01:38:27.000
That's not gonna happen.

1239
01:38:27.000 --> 01:38:30.000
And you know it.

1240
01:38:34.000 --> 01:38:37.000
I don't want that either.

1241
01:38:40.000 --> 01:38:44.000
You really think you can
outrun what you are?

1242
01:38:45.000 --> 01:38:49.000
We are who we are, Mason.

1243
01:38:50.000 --> 01:38:53.000
I have been given complete
autonomy

1244
01:38:53.000 --> 01:38:56.000
to make Black Kites
stronger than ever.

1245
01:38:56.000 --> 01:39:01.000
I want you with me...
by my side, as we were.

1246
01:39:04.000 --> 01:39:09.000
You're the very reason I
didn't pull the trigger ten years ago.

1247
01:39:11.000 --> 01:39:13.000
And why I have to now.

1248
01:39:14.000 --> 01:39:16.000
[body falls with a thud]

1249
01:39:16.000 --> 01:39:19.000
[sinister music]

1250
01:39:34.000 --> 01:39:37.000
[people chattering happily]

1251
01:39:47.000 --> 01:39:49.000
[soft music]

1252
01:39:52.000 --> 01:39:55.000
What's up? Anything new?

1253
01:39:55.000 --> 01:39:58.000
Just having some cocoa
and reading a book.

1254
01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:01.000
Zoom in and up-res.

1255
01:40:01.000 --> 01:40:04.000
[computer bleeping]

1256
01:40:07.000 --> 01:40:09.000
Er, maybe we should
start exploring

1257
01:40:09.000 --> 01:40:11.000
other ways to find him.

1258
01:40:11.000 --> 01:40:14.000
He hid from us for
ten years...

1259
01:40:14.000 --> 01:40:16.000
until her.

1260
01:40:17.000 --> 01:40:19.000
It's a matter of when.

1261
01:40:27.000 --> 01:40:29.000
Deakins: Wait.

1262
01:40:35.000 --> 01:40:37.000
It's him.

1263
01:40:48.000 --> 01:40:51.000
Your friend said this was
for you.

1264
01:40:56.000 --> 01:40:59.000
[packet rustles]

1265
01:41:12.000 --> 01:41:15.000
- Where is he?
- He was there a moment ago.

1266
01:41:16.000 --> 01:41:19.000
[dramatic music]

1267
01:41:30.000 --> 01:41:34.000
[music playing]

1268
01:41:49.000 --> 01:41:52.000
[singer vocalizing]

1269
01:43:16.000 --> 01:43:19.000
[music fades]

1270
01:43:20.000 --> 01:43:23.000
[dramatic music playing]

1271
01:45:38.000 --> 01:45:42.000
[music fades]

1272
01:45:43.000 --> 01:45:46.000
[suspenseful music playing]

1273
01:47:14.000 --> 01:47:19.000
[music ends]

